# Code strings (ST5): the inside is X_eTaL, drawn as code (a pipeline's
# |> as a triangle, a label as a small one); c"..." takes the usual
# escapes, c#"..."# is verbatim. The value is the same Char vector as a
# plain string of the same text, and fmt keeps the form.
== SOURCE
p := c"n_eg x |> f_ $h"
q := c#"p_rint! "a""#
p m_atch "n_eg x |> f_ $h"
t_ally q
== TOKENS
0..1 Var(p)
2..4 Assign
5..23 Code("n_eg x |> f_ $h")
23..24 Newline
24..25 Var(q)
26..28 Assign
29..45 Code("p_rint! \"a\"")
45..46 Newline
46..47 Var(p)
48..54 Func(m_atch)
55..72 Str("n_eg x |> f_ $h")
72..73 Newline
73..79 Func(t_ally)
80..81 Var(q)
== RENDER
p ← c"n̲eg x ▷ f̲ ▹h"
q ← c#"p̲rint! "a""#
p m̲atch "n_eg x |> f_ $h"
t̲ally q
== CANONICAL
p := c"n_eg x |> f_ $h"
q := c#"p_rint! "a""#
(p m_atch "n_eg x |> f_ $h")
(t_ally q)
== RESULT
1
11
